1
00:00:00,708 --> 00:00:05,960
This child has muscle wasting and mosaic
variegated aneuploidy, a condition in which

2
00:00:05,920 --> 00:00:08,440
cells can carry different numbers of
chromosomes.

3
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:12,760
Our question is whether an existing medicine
could improve muscle function while

4
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:15,240
preserving the cells needed for growth and
repair.

5
00:00:15,489 --> 00:00:18,280
We propose two medicines for laboratory
testing.

6
00:00:19,882 --> 00:00:24,560
Our leading genetic explanation involves
BUB1B, the gene that makes the

7
00:00:24,440 --> 00:00:27,200
chromosome-checking protein BUBR1.

8
00:00:27,456 --> 00:00:29,760
One change creates an early stop.

9
00:00:29,766 --> 00:00:31,920
The other changes one amino acid.

10
00:00:32,165 --> 00:00:36,720
We still need to establish whether they occupy
opposite gene copies, and whether the

11
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:38,960
altered protein retains useful function.

12
00:00:40,597 --> 00:00:43,360
Our first hypothesis is everolimus.

13
00:00:43,479 --> 00:00:47,920
It inhibits mTORC1, a pathway that regulates
cell growth.

14
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:52,400
Its established target and pediatric use make
it practical to investigate.

15
00:00:52,743 --> 00:00:58,080
A different BUB1B mouse model showed increased
pathway activity, but tested no drug

16
00:00:57,960 --> 00:00:58,640
rescue.

17
00:00:58,833 --> 00:01:02,880
We must establish harmful excess signaling and
useful muscle benefit.

18
00:01:04,478 --> 00:01:08,120
Our challenger is niacin, the nicotinic acid
medicine.

19
00:01:08,309 --> 00:01:12,200
It increased muscle NAD in a small study of
another disease.

20
00:01:12,465 --> 00:01:18,520
Separate experiments connect NAD and the
enzyme SIRT2 to BUBR1 stability.

21
00:01:18,782 --> 00:01:23,160
The missing link is whether niacin restores
useful protein and muscle function in this

22
00:01:23,040 --> 00:01:23,880
genotype.

23
00:01:24,077 --> 00:01:25,800
We test the medicines separately.

24
00:01:27,434 --> 00:01:31,080
Our completed computer model shows why
percentages can mislead.

25
00:01:31,431 --> 00:01:36,200
In one assumed scenario, removing abnormal
cells improved the chromosome-normal

26
00:01:36,080 --> 00:01:39,560
fraction while reducing total muscle-cell
output over time.

27
00:01:39,919 --> 00:01:42,680
These are simulated results, not drug effects.

28
00:01:43,063 --> 00:01:47,880
Our experiment therefore follows each starting
cell, including those that die or stop

29
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:48,440
dividing.

30
00:01:49,976 --> 00:01:54,640
We would compare affected and genetically
corrected muscle models, using measured drug

31
00:01:54,520 --> 00:01:55,440
exposures.

32
00:01:55,799 --> 00:02:00,800
A medicine must improve either existing muscle
or new muscle production, preserve the

33
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:03,600
other, and avoid worsening chromosome errors.

34
00:02:03,959 --> 00:02:06,800
Independent confirmation must reproduce the
result.

35
00:02:07,074 --> 00:02:11,280
The cancer history also requires checking that
neither medicine helps tumor cells

36
00:02:11,160 --> 00:02:13,840
survive or interferes with cancer treatment.

37
00:02:15,474 --> 00:02:20,000
Arimoclomol remains a reserve because rescue
of this protein is unproved.

38
00:02:20,337 --> 00:02:25,600
Removing senescent cells has strong genetic
mouse evidence, but some drugs also damage

39
00:02:25,480 --> 00:02:26,880
repair in young muscle.

40
00:02:26,992 --> 00:02:29,280
We investigate that mechanism in parallel.

41
00:02:29,468 --> 00:02:34,080
Transcript rescue and other alternatives have
explicit promotion tests in our report.

42
00:02:35,658 --> 00:02:40,840
We have completed sequence review, evidence
review and computational study design.

43
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:43,640
No biological drug experiment has run.

44
00:02:43,883 --> 00:02:47,160
We seek a consented cell model and laboratory
partner.

45
00:02:47,509 --> 00:02:51,960
The deliverable is a reproducible decision:
advance a medicine with measured

46
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:55,000
functional benefit, or explain why none
passes.

47
00:02:55,313 --> 00:02:59,080
The method can then be tested in other
chromosome-instability disorders.
